@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Fix :class:`~filelock.ReadWriteLock` acting on ``-journal``, ``-wal`` or ``-shm`` files another process puts beside its
+database in a directory other accounts can write: a write could land in another file, a reader could get in beside a
+writer, and an acquire could fail. SQLite now opens the database by name only in a directory no other account can write,
+and through a private hard link elsewhere. A database whose schema takes more than a few kilobytes to load raises
+:class:`ValueError` instead of running past the acquire timeout.
